# What this file is for: the language GitHub reports for this repository, and
# the diffs it shows.
#
# Measured, before any of the rules below (tracked bytes):
#
#   package-lock.json    186,504
#   Taskfile YAML        238,864   in 25 module Taskfiles
#   Markdown             171,194   of which 48,641 a frozen CHANGELOG
#   CI and hook YAML      43,526   .github/ and lefthook
#   demo/                 27,395   a worked example, of which 3,177 Go
#   release.config.cjs     1,373
#
# What GitHub actually reported, with the previous version of this file in
# place:
#
#   {"JavaScript": 1373}
#
# One semantic-release config and nothing else — the language bar read 100%
# JavaScript off 1.4 KB, against 239 KB of the Taskfiles this repository
# exists to publish. The rule meant to fix that,
#
#   *.yaml linguist-language=YAML
#
# could not, and had not. linguist-language overrides the language a file is
# counted AS; it does not make that language countable. The bar counts only
# languages Linguist types `programming` or `markup`, YAML is typed `data`,
# and renaming YAML to YAML leaves the type alone. linguist-detectable is the
# attribute that overrides it.

# ─── Counted: the Taskfiles ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The 239 KB this repository is. linguist-detectable is what puts a `data`
# language on the bar; see above for why linguist-language could not.
*.yaml linguist-detectable=true

# ─── Not counted: CI and hook configuration ──────────────────────────────
# .github/workflows, the issue templates, dependabot and lefthook: 43,526
# bytes describing how this repository is built, not what it is. Every one of
# them is *.yml, nothing here makes *.yml detectable, and so they stay off the
# bar without a rule. Written down because the split is load-bearing — a later
# `*.yml linguist-detectable=true` would undo it, and would look like tidying.

# ─── Generated ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Solver output for a single devDependency, 186 KB of it. Reviewed as "the
# lock moved", not line by line.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true

# CHANGELOG.md gets no rule, though its 48,641 bytes look the part. It is not
# output: RELEASE.md calls it a frozen historical record through 5.4.0, the
# last version cut by hand, and it has not moved since the automation landed.
# Release notes are built from merged pull requests now — see
# .github/release.yml. So there is no diff to collapse, and Markdown is prose,
# which the bar leaves out regardless. Marking it generated would only be a
# claim about the file that is not true.

# ─── Documentation: the worked example ───────────────────────────────────
# demo/ is a consumer of this library kept runnable so the README's claims
# stay honest: a Go binary, a Dockerfile, two Helm charts and a kind config.
# Linguist already keeps it off the bar — it reported no Go at all for this
# repository, though demo/ holds 3,177 bytes of it. Stating that here makes it
# a decision rather than a coincidence, and keeps the rule at the top of this
# file from pulling demo/deploy's 5,488 bytes of chart YAML onto the bar
# alongside the Taskfiles.
demo/** linguist-documentation=true
